<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mass burial reveals hidden toll of Algeria’s deadly ‘Black Wednesday’ wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4dee0e90303c601b4f0d4e24a9afd16cfdb6b83a1c43cbfe59e80abee8c1dd7</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260904-mass-burial-algeria-black-wednesday-deadly-wildfires--e2ca45613885.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260904-mass-burial-algeria-black-wednesday-deadly-wildfires" /><summary type="html">Wildfires ripped across northeastern Algeria in late August. Photos and videos showing the mass burial of several dozen people have raised questions about the real death toll of the fires as Algerian authorities haven’t shared new numbers since August 26. A number of Moroccan social media accounts have also been sharing disinformation about the fires.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Pragmatic international relations': Sánchez seeks to avoid 'further conflict with Rabat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d5afa2a8d2fbd2ea3e2529c6fd82282726506b1f618d07e8e25bd67395ecf97</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T05:22:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s_nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat--c4a5b9cb15c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s%C3%A1nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Alana Moceri, International Relations Professor at IE School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs. The migrant crossings at Ceuta have become both a domestic and international political lightning rod. At home, Pedro Sánchez faces opponents who can cast migration in existential terms, with Spain's far right amplifying the rhetoric of "invasion." Internationally, the crisis exposes the geopolitical leverage inherent in control of the border. Ceuta thus emerges as more than a migration crisis: the border becomes at once an instrument of geopolitical leverage, a weapon in Spain's domestic political contest, and a battleground for competing narratives and disinformation.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisia top court upholds long sentences in mass trial of opposition figures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:607595261303c65bc016d27a375d74a2902cc4ebeb2c0fd04ce0eb9efbcc0916</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T22:17:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260903-tunisia-court-upholds-prison-sentences-of-up-to-45-years-for-opposition-figures--25780c534aec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260903-tunisia-court-upholds-prison-sentences-of-up-to-45-years-for-opposition-figures" /><summary type="html">Tunisia's top court on Thursday upheld prison sentences of up to 45 years for opposition leaders, lawyers and businessmen convicted in a major conspiracy case, in a ruling opponents said further entrenches President Kais Saied's authoritarian rule.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Shady surgeons and Nigeria organ harvesting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba28adc2084bfa6377f30c13bca9bab68ae47939922ec28147b6571ea33fbd4d</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T20:15:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/shady-surgeons-and-nigeria-organ-harvesting--d87a92aad99d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/shady-surgeons-and-nigeria-organ-harvesting" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Legal loopholes and gaps about specialised medicine may be driving illegal organ harvesting in Nigeria. Also, South Sudan may be moving closer to delivering on elections scheduled for December. Finally, on the islands of São Tomé and Príncipe, six colonial-era plantation estates have just been added to the UNESCO World Heritage List.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia water crisis deepens as temperatures approach 50°C</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11666dfbe8e9059765e60267d682f2f668cc16e443639c54ed1718a3093be443</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:52:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-water-crisis-deepens-as-temperatures-approach-50_c--25ad983d7cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-water-crisis-deepens-as-temperatures-approach-50%C2%B0c" /><summary type="html">In Tunisia, powerful heatwaves are driving power cuts and water shortage. While the country has been dealing with structural water scarcity and recurring drought for years, the current crisis is fuelling anger against the government, even as authorities attempt to coordinate water distribution efforts to quell the crisis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan editor found safe after abduction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcfeacc90bcdf8035ccbe41bae25f96f99b45b0d1db0c4a853cc44e5aa2c17a3</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction--7cd7d68f36ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Media rights groups in Kenya call for an investigation after a top journalist is abducted overnight by heavily armed men. Also, trials for three potential vaccines against the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola are due to start over the next couple of months. Plus Senegalese consumers who are frustrated by the rising cost of living have launched a new campaign.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1b78abbb06a4251d2283a8237e3f87f3bbfa61c3d44baf5ad2e736daa47a788</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:20:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush--02ef226c47f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan security forces displayed "total permissiveness" during last month's massive wave of migrants who crossed into the Spanish North African territory of Ceuta, according to a Spanish police report seen by a French news agency on Wednesday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>IMF reaches historical loan agreement with Senegal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71b9f3ed7793a6b88c701b14afff3568d74fd88702b119a4d626199c699df1d2</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:51:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/imf-reaches-historical-loan-agreement-with-senegal--2eb64631acbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/imf-reaches-historical-loan-agreement-with-senegal" /><summary type="html">The IMF and Senegal have agreed on a new 2.2 billion-dollar loan programme to support financial reforms, a relief for the country after a huge amount of unreported debt recently came to light. The president has accused his predecessor of hiding the true state of the country's imbalanced budget deficit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya shifts to electric cars as fuel prices soar 50%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8167e054380aea2acab39729415349ed639cf68033fef335498ae665035b43c2</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T11:19:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-kenya-shifts-to-electric-cars-as-fuel-prices-soar-50--214cc24f9987.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-kenya-shifts-to-electric-cars-as-fuel-prices-soar-50" /><summary type="html">In Kenya, locally made eletric vehicles are gaining traction as fuel prices rise. As more and more Kenyans consider going electric, local firms are stepping up to assemble EV's domestically.</summary></entry><entry><title>Illegal mining ravages Johannesburg neighbourhoods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:641a47ed265d53dfdef5b4b13c3adf9331b6f11f4434bb38e751a759ca098dfa</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T11:14:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-illegal-mining-ravages-johannesburg-neighbourhoods--a75e47943773.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-illegal-mining-ravages-johannesburg-neighbourhoods" /><summary type="html">Some houses in one Johannesburg neighbourhood are in danger of collapse because of illegal mining. Known as Zama Zamas, around 34,000 illegal miners are thought to be working in South Africa, in the hope of finding gold and chromium. The mines they dig hollow out the ground, which causes buildings to collapse as well as frequent power outages.</summary></entry><entry><title>Military buildup seen in Ethiopia near Sudanese border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47abcaa39598f4e99d0611e4d7b272588622deb7c72b438b3058c1b55d32b3b5</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T10:57:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-military-buildup-seen-in-ethiopia-near-sudanese-border--3f84da8e9b1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-military-buildup-seen-in-ethiopia-near-sudanese-border" /><summary type="html">A major military buildup has been observed on the Ethiopian side of the Sudanese border. It comes amid intensified fighting between the Sudanese armed forces and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF). Sudan and Ethiopia have both accused each other of supporting rebels within their borders.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africans missing in Nepal's glacial flood</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5188de0934d2ca64aa00c88f7bb4645e91f31d68343d10a07fb651f09819736</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africans-missing-in-nepal-s-glacial-flood--856bd6e9f51b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-missing-in-nepal-s-glacial-flood" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Africa Disaster Relief is looking for six South Africans who went missing in the deadly floods on the border between Nepal and China. Also, South African illegal miners are undermining their own communities. Finally, rising fuel prices are pushing Kenyans towards electric vehicles.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Niger's thwarted mutiny highlights junta's dependence on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de624b5e4d0b23aed4905df76de622fbe37eec08740daa0b1c7fecd66ac1507e</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260901-what-russia-helping-niger-junta-stop-mutiny-means-for-its-sovereignty--ec75ac36d492.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260901-what-russia-helping-niger-junta-stop-mutiny-means-for-its-sovereignty" /><summary type="html">A failed mutiny in Niger over the weekend shows how important Russia's Africa Corps mercenaries are in the country, according to analysts. They argue that the failed mutiny on Saturday shows how the country's security landscape has worsened and contradicts claims from Niger's junta about the country's independence from foreign powers.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ghana cocoa farmers reject new 'punitive' land conversion law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ccc67a45d1fbd7cd594d8c54a2cf3a1a96895512128d9399bec82fea13e5a8</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:05:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-ghana-cocoa-farmers-reject-new-punitive-land-conversion-law--206a8b9097ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-ghana-cocoa-farmers-reject-new-punitive-land-conversion-law" /><summary type="html">Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. President Mahama says supporting local processing is the key to economic growth. Cocoa chiefs say that the changes still leave the sector resting on an outdated colonial model.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's opposition rejects president's dialogue offer and calls for demonstration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da79fc5ef5c799eb9adf876e471eaf253cc1f018a023f365d148182baca3d57d</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:40:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-dr-congo-s-opposition-rejects-president-s-dialogue-offer-and-calls-for-demonstration--b2e303a5a5e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-dr-congo-s-opposition-rejects-president-s-dialogue-offer-and-calls-for-demonstration" /><summary type="html">In DR Congo, managing the spread of Ebola is made all the more difficult as the country is juggling simultaneous security crises including untangling a peace deal with M23 rebels. President Felix Tshisekedi offered to convene a national dialogue which opposition parties call a smoke screen hiding an attempted power grab.</summary></entry><entry><title>As capital goes back to normal, Niger downplays soldiers' mutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef539a0ccbb0109a914c6af0484bcf17d8757ed9f0111dab5c52c1459db7c48d</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:51:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-as-capital-goes-back-to-normal-niger-downplays-soldiers-mutiny--e59d539f0a3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-as-capital-goes-back-to-normal-niger-downplays-soldiers-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Niger's capital is back to normal after an intense week-end. A soldier mutiny took over Niamey on August 29, which was stopped by the army alongside the Russian paramilitary Africa Corps. The next day, Algeria sent four fighters aircrafts and two other military planes as cooperation with Nigeria is recently back on : an unexpected decision. Since it got independence, Algeria's non intervention doctrine is part of its DNA. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard tells us more about the goal of this decision.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's iconic Sidi Bou Said town added to UNESCO world heritage list</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d968522897eb01b8115de9d21df4691344efe24c0962eb376987bb05d9ab76f0</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-iconic-sidi-bou-said-town-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-list--114022c5711c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-iconic-sidi-bou-said-town-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-list" /><summary type="html">In Tunisia, UNESCO recognised the town of Sidi Bou Said as a world heritage site this July. The designation marks a new period in the cultural preservation of this historic tourist site. The special status may help as it battles erosion, like in the floods this last January, but it will also help boost its lesser known Sufi mystical traditions. FRANCE 24's Lilia Blaise and Hamdi Tlili were there to report on the Kharja ceremonies, which run in the town from mid-august til the end of September.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan airport staff strike delays thousands of passengers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebc12222f3de8463d2789625f3439c10ca6e9282d2e8d6e1824dbc9731ec26d1</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:20:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-airport-staff-strike-delays-thousands-of-passengers--de2fae5b8da6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-airport-staff-strike-delays-thousands-of-passengers" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A workers' strike at Kenya's main airport leaves travellers grounded. Also, Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. And in Tunisia, the picturesque town of Sidi Bou Saïd has been recognised by UNESCO as being important to global heritage.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Niger junta puts down mutiny with help from Russia's Africa Corps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36f63138f07cdc286f0eaecf94736c2603103fcf6429712e7db19c2026376fb1</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:20:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny--b57d1305a2a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Life returned to normal in Niger's capital on Sunday, a day after mutineers stormed both the presidential palace and a military base at Niamey's main airport, resisting forces loyal to the ruling junta until Russia’s Africa Corps intervened. State TV reported that dozens of soldiers were killed or arrested, with some paraded in front of cameras live on television.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Niger: Junta says back in control after mutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57e04a6195f082a72979f3e0a86aab6e1d56c3d6b2b4f75de80c28022dafdecc</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny--b01e157aa8c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Gunfire and explosions have been reported in Niger, as mutinying soldiers attempted to storm the presidential palace in the capital, Niamey, in a challenge to the ruling junta. The government said it had regained control after hours of fighting on Saturday. Léo Paichard and Nick Rushworth report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger's junta says 'regaining control' after clashes in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a24aaa8581487764b1c8f60bcce1cc27acbdb2c2bb5b9f5414fc9f9b6395af9f</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/niger-s-junta-says-regaining-control-after-clashes-in-capital--2bf7e08a1a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/niger-s-junta-says-regaining-control-after-clashes-in-capital" /><summary type="html">Niger's ​defense ​ministry said the armed forces were ​progressively ‌retaking ⁠control ‌of sites targeted in ⁠an overnight attack on ​the ‌capital Niamey, according to a ‌statement read ​on state television, which resumed broadcasting ​on ​Saturday after ​temporarily going ​offline.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger junta regains control after mutiny with help from Russian paramilitary forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbc46e26f4788839cd22743c9e7814bf8d57c637819981ccbb3bf417c6f0a87e</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T06:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260829-gunfire-and-explosions-heard-near-military-base-in-niger-s-capital--2f45acce54fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260829-gunfire-and-explosions-heard-near-military-base-in-niger-s-capital" /><summary type="html">Niger's junta said Saturday it was back in control after mutineers held soldiers hostage at a military base next to the capital's airport. Russian Africa Corps paramilitary forces helped members of Niger's presidential guard recapture the air base, killing some of the mutineers, according to diplomatic and security sources.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi calls for national dialogue excluding M23 rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364bb0fcfc1049ad3cd8ec5263c51bb39612b6eb70362a6ad8e6636c610e96cd</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T20:36:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260828-drc-president-tshisekedi-calls-for-national-dialogue-excluding-m23-rebels--ac8f13394274.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260828-drc-president-tshisekedi-calls-for-national-dialogue-excluding-m23-rebels" /><summary type="html">In the Democratic Republic of Congo, President Félix Tshisekedi calls for a national dialogue to ease tensions, while excluding M23 rebels from taking part, as the government plans to suspend 11 public universities in rebel-controlled areas.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda's King of Tooro, once world's youngest reigning monarch, dies at 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2efd1f07a8288929872591b66187fc9236c0c18ff607aef97a9aa7dcc8d975a3</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260828-uganda-s-king-of-tooro-once-world-s-youngest-reigning-monarch-dies-at-34--48846a82350f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260828-uganda-s-king-of-tooro-once-world-s-youngest-reigning-monarch-dies-at-34" /><summary type="html">King Oyo Nyimba, leader of the Tooro kingdom in western Uganda, has died at the age of 34, the region's prime minister of his kingdom announced Thursday. Crowned at three years old, he became the world's youngest reigning monarch in 1995.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's lucrative business of kidnappings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72e793dcc57e73d6b0db118e2c7f3b50be0736b4a6e3c1b2643e7ef25a5ffd6c</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T20:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-the-lucrative-business-of-kidnappings--b7681c405c06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-the-lucrative-business-of-kidnappings" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, we speak to a Lagos analyst behind a new report laying out the figures behind abductions. Also, Tanzania's ruling party kicks the vice-president out even after he announces his plans to step down next week. Finally, in Senegal, the first African-manufactured generic drug to treat sickle cell disease is raising hopes of better treatment and reduced reliance on costly imported medicine.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Wildfires kill 12 in Algeria as severe heatwave sweeps North Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aefeb067e4600622ddf6c41e448b21cde83b7a4f210c10d3e3ecc189a2763bb</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T23:46:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260826-wildfires-algeria-severe-heatwave-sweeps-north-africa--aed0a3051f42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260826-wildfires-algeria-severe-heatwave-sweeps-north-africa" /><summary type="html">Twelve people died and dozens were injured as wildfires tore through northern Algeria on Wednesday, with authorities battling more than 150 blazes amid a scorching heatwave sweeping across North Africa. Six of the 54 injured were in critical condition and receiving intensive care.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>New revelations at South Africa corruption inquiry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2730cf0044a74483cc0ccd134b667df7dcb331b0c0991f70cb2efb380dbf6f30</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T20:48:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-kingpin-and-the-corruption-commission--d0c22de924b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-kingpin-and-the-corruption-commission" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: The three-day testimony of an alleged underworld kingpin exposes the deep links between alleged criminals and high-profile police officers in South Africa. Also, in Tunisia, grieving families bid farewell to the young victims of a boat that went down in the Mediterranean Sea over the weekend. Finally, in an era of mass production and electric machines, one young Kenyan fashion designer is taking a slower approach.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Mawlid festivities cancelled in Tigray over drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da101c9e82d3c30ceb09d4ae6c413812a7380ea447d1298a125f2a866c153990</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T20:45:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mawlid-cancelled-in-tigray--668d53805925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mawlid-cancelled-in-tigray" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Muslims celebrate Mawlid across Africa but festivities are cancelled in Tigray because of recent drone attacks. But first: the United States calls for beefed-up UN sanctions against the warring parties in Sudan. Finally, in the Kenyan village of Cheporor, a recent discovery of gold sends thousands of amateur prospectors rushing to the area.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria’s president orders rescue operation after mass kidnapping at mosque</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb4df752f6f31cd6f8af7a5cce6900e17b32273d9426aab6d6456397926f34c4</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T17:10:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260825-nigeria-president-orders-rescue-after-mass-kidnapping-during-mosque-attack--e37e32f460dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260825-nigeria-president-orders-rescue-after-mass-kidnapping-during-mosque-attack" /><summary type="html">Nigerian President Bola Tinubu on Tuesday ordered security agencies to conduct a rescue operation after the mass kidnapping of worshippers during an attack on a mosque in the north-central Niger State last week. Local authorities were still trying to verify the number of missing people, but local residents said roughly 600 women, children and elderly people had been abducted.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Meet the young Kenyan designer preserving culture through traditional craft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:382a7d6a53508de64072a9289d543b8bc8ef3edffa9ed962c14c8375c6934e15</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:47:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T12:19:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-meet-the-young-kenyan-designer-preserving-culture-through-traditional-craft--56285aab4f82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-meet-the-young-kenyan-designer-preserving-culture-through-traditional-craft" /><summary type="html">At a time when fashion is increasingly dominated by mass production, a young Kenyan designer is taking a slower approach. Hillary Mukabwa, the founder and lead designer of Mukabwa Studio in Nairobi, works with hand looms to create cotton fabrics that he turns into clothes, bags and more in a deliberate attempt to reconnect with a craft increasingly being pushed aside by modernisation.</summary></entry></feed>
